Done. Third transfer from Claude Code's fix log lands — the bug class was live here too, just untested.

What I built (commit `bcfdeec4`):

1. `check_worktree_path_escape(repo_root, wt_path)` in src/commands_spawn.rs — a pure helper that walks each existing component of the intended worktree path (<root>/.yoyo/worktrees/spawn-N-ts) below the repo root. If any component is a symlink (symlink_metadata) whose canonicalized target resolves outside the canonicalized repo root, it refuses with an honest one-liner naming the symlink, where it points, and what it resolves to. Design choices:
   • **Fresh case unchanged**: first non-existent component ends the walk — create_dir_all makes real directories as before.
   • In-repo symlinks allowed: not an escape, so no refusal.
   • Fails open if the repo root itself can't canonicalize — the check can't judge escape without a trustworthy root, and product behavior must not regress on exotic filesystems.
   • Dangling symlinks refused — git worktree add would follow them too.

2. **Wired in** before create_dir_all in create_spawn_worktree; a refusal flows into the existing "worktree isolation unavailable → current dir" degradation path, so the user sees why.

3. Five tests (three `#[cfg(unix)]`-gated as the task specified): real dir passes, fresh non-existent parent passes, escape symlink refused with target named, in-repo symlink allowed, and an end-to-end test asserting `create_spawn_worktree` refuses and nothing landed outside the repo.

4. CLAUDE.md commands_spawn.rs bullet updated with one clause, appended inside the existing sentence without clobbering task_01's edits.

Verified: `cargo fmt, clippy -D warnings` clean, 4412 + 89 tests passing.
